  "name": "Steel articles subject to 50% Section 232 duty (Proclamation 10896 as amended by Proclamation 11021)",
  "source": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/04/09/2026-06960/strengthening-actions-taken-to-adjust-imports-of-aluminum-steel-and-copper-into-the-united-states",
  "source_original": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2025/03/05/2025-03598/implementation-of-duties-on-steel-pursuant-to-proclamation-10896-adjusting-imports-of-steel-into-the",
  "notes": [
    "Rate applies to articles entirely or almost entirely made of steel (Chapters 72–73), on full customs value.",
    "Proclamation 11021 (April 2, 2026, effective April 6, 2026) restructured S232 tariffs into tiers:",
    "  50% — articles entirely/almost entirely of steel (this file)",
    "  25% — derivative steel articles substantially made of steel (see steel_aluminum_copper_derivatives_04_02_2026.json)",
    "  15% — fixed industrial machinery, grid equipment, and (per Proclamation 11032 effective June 8, 2026) agricultural and mobile industrial equipment",
    "  10% — articles using ≥85% US-melted and poured steel by weight (threshold lowered from 95% by Proclamation 11032)",
    "Codes from Chapters 84, 85, 87, 94 that appeared in the original file have been reclassified as 25% derivative steel articles per Proclamation 11021.",
    "Codes 7321–7324 (cooking appliances, heaters, household articles, sinks/baths) and specific 7326 codes (73269035, 73269045) have also been moved to the 25% derivatives file per Annex I-B verification."
  ],
